{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/318802-2ed-fan-idea-frailties-as-persistent-conditions","id":318802,"title":"2ed Fan Idea: Frailties as Persistent Conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-22T01:52:57-08:00","id":318802,"title":"2ed Fan Idea: Frailties as Persistent Conditions","content":"I'm preparing to run <b>Changeling</b> game on GMC rules update and got idea for it that I think could be neat for 2ed <b>CtL</b> in general. As werewolves will get Totem Aspirations and mages will get Obsessions as special variant of Aspirations systems, maybe changeling will get their Frailties like a special Persistent Conditions? You would get extra Beats by confronting the weaknesses the Wyrd is imposing on you. And character could change them, if they Wyrd evolution would dictating they can left behind they old Frailties. They just replace the Condition with other one<br /> <br /> Like a Darkling ha Frailties on mistletoe. But in the game, he was forced and accepted the mistletoe as the Token of his beloved Fairest loved. He gets an extra Beat for &quot;solving&quot; his Frailty, but bow character changeling need to change this old on the sheet for the new one. Maybe now the amber will be his Frailty, because his Fairest girlfriend has amber eyes?<br /> <br /> What do you think about this idea, guys? Is it sounds good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T12:56:33-08:00","id":319196,"title":"","content":"That sounds pretty cool. I'd be down with Frailties-as-Conditions. Makes sense logically, plus it incentivizes players to choose Frailties that have a good chance of actually coming into play. Incidentally, <i>Oathbound</i> would also make a decent Condition, methinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T16:20:46-08:00","id":319490,"title":"","content":"I suggest that Frailties are indeed Condition but are resolved when you lower your Wyrd enough to lose them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T00:11:29-08:00","id":319690,"title":"","content":"You can lower Wyrd on your own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T00:24:37-08:00","id":319695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quo